e_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1379478-superiors-in-the-trinity-continuum-era?p=1380404#post1380404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go for Paragons. They are human with a bit more, but nothing really supernatural, they are Just extremely good in what humans can possibly do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like Paragons. Parahumans is a term that I prefer to reserve for human variants, whereas I tend to see Superiors as human upgrades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-11-2020, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:23:20-07:00","id":1380414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1379478-superiors-in-the-trinity-continuum-era?p=1380407#post1380407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like Paragons. Parahumans is a term that I prefer to reserve for human variants, whereas I tend to see Superiors as human upgrades.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YES! Paragons fit a modern Stalwart quite well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:31:44-07:00","id":1380444,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz That works too. In one of the old D&amp;D worlds (I think it\u2019s Mystara) they have a thing for high level wizards called the Path of the Paragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:17:49-07:00","id":1380460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1379478-superiors-in-the-trinity-continuum-era?p=1380444#post1380444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz That works too. In one of the old D&amp;D worlds (I think it\u2019s Mystara) they have a thing for high level wizards called the Path of the Paragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paragon is one of the words I learned in RPG that have no use in real world (for me at least), but with a really awesome meaning.<br /> <br /> If I am not wrong one of the paths to Immortality in D&amp;D (BASMI, never remember the 2, 3 and 4 leters) was the path of Paragon, there was 3 other paths, Polymath, Epic Hero, and another. I am quite sure it is the origin for that thing you are talking. It has been a long time since I read this book, but they are available in Drivethru if I am not wrong.<br /> <br /> Also:<br /> There is a D&amp;D 3e book called Unearthed Arcana (or Arcana Unearthed, what ever) that have a kind o prestige class for each of the basic races, Human Paragon, Elf Paragon, Halfling Paragon, etc, that basically increase their race characteristics.<br /> There is also a Mutants and Masterminds called Paragons that is basically a regular world were suddenly some people started getting powers (much like aberrant), but with some weird dream/arcadia reason for that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:37:35-07:00","id":1380491,"title":"","content":"Mutants &amp; Masterminds' Paragon book was excellent, and my initial description of it was &quot;This is what Aberrant should have been.&quot; A basic framework for how and why powers work, and why they've suddenly appeared, with a vast array of optional characters and organizations you can use or discard to build the setting the way you want it to be. Steve Kenson was going to be the developer for new Aberrant 1st ed books before Arthaus pulled the plug on it way back when, and it was obvious that a lot of his thoughts about Aberrant went into Paragons. It's one of the reasons I'm excited he's involved with TC:Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T15:55:52-07:00","id":1380508,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24020_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24020\" data-vbnamecard=\"24020\">Mateus</a> Luz thanks \ud83d\ude0a. I meant the Wrath of the Immortals setting. Me and my friends played that for a couple months back in junior high. I never tried Mutants and Masterminds.","signatu